    "historical_decision": "Banate of Bosnia and Kingdom of Bosnia are rank/state-form phases of the same medieval Bosnian state identity. Tvrtko I is continuously described as Bosnian ban 1353-1377 and king 1377-1391; his October 1377 coronation elevated the Bosnian state to royal rank rather than replacing it with a successor state.",
    "activity_rule": "Keep Tvrtko's Ban and King Activities separate because his sovereign title changed, while relinking all Banate-era Activities to one continuous Kingdom of Bosnia polity identity.",
    "boundary_note": "The Banate designation begins at 1180 only as the earliest currently modeled ATLAS Ban-of-Bosnia Activity coverage floor (Kulin), not as a claim that the banate began in 1180. The royal phase begins on 26 October 1377, the coronation date preserved by the Museum of the Bosnian Kingdom chronology."
  },
